{"id":"ee11792e-6dc8-4390-abf7-a8b1fd62590c","revision":0,"last_node_id":37,"last_link_id":65,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-460],"size":[3760,400],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Camera angles by prompt — every character turned 45° at a time (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nTwo character pictures turned round in 45° steps: the original (0°), a three-quarter front view (45°), the side profile (90°), a three-quarter back view (135°) and the back (180°). Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo draws every angle; one **Compare Viewer** flips through them, and its branch chip shows *All*, *Mei* or *Kai*.\n\n1. **Characters** is a Load Media with one group per character (`# Mei`, `# Kai`): one branch each, named.\n2. **Angle instructions** holds one line per angle; **Prompt Template** (*zip*) adds *keep the same subject, clothes, colours, lighting and art style*. **Cross Reference** pairs every character with every instruction, two **Tree to Data** feed *image 1* and the prompt — 8 edits.\n3. **Construct Tree** puts the edits back into one branch per character; **Merge** puts each original in front of its angles.\n4. **Labels** names the columns of the **Image Grid**, the files of **Save by Path** (`output/arbor/angles/0 · Mei/90°.png`) and the slides of the **Compare Viewer** (*Mei · 90°*) — one list serves both characters.\n\nWrite angles as views of the subject (\"Side profile view…\"), not as camera moves — the model may draw a camera. It does not reliably tell its left from its right, so the template stops at 180°. Add an angle by adding a line to both panels; use your own pictures with **Add…** on Load Media."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Camera angles by prompt — every character turned 45° at a time (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo edit)\n\nTwo character pictures turned round in 45° steps: the original (0°), a three-quarter front view (45°), the side profile (90°), a three-quarter back view (135°) and the back (180°). Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo draws every angle; one **Compare Viewer** flips through them, and its branch chip shows *All*, *Mei* or *Kai*.\n\n1. **Characters** is a Load Media with one group per character (`# Mei`, `# Kai`): one branch each, named.\n2. **Angle instructions** holds one line per angle; **Prompt Template** (*zip*) adds *keep the same subject, clothes, colours, lighting and art style*. **Cross Reference** pairs every character with every instruction, two **Tree to Data** feed *image 1* and the prompt — 8 edits.\n3. **Construct Tree** puts the edits back into one branch per character; **Merge** puts each original in front of its angles.\n4. **Labels** names the columns of the **Image Grid**, the files of **Save by Path** (`output/arbor/angles/0 · Mei/90°.png`) and the slides of the **Compare Viewer** (*Mei · 90°*) — one list serves both characters.\n\nWrite angles as views of the subject (\"Side profile view…\"), not as camera moves — the model may draw a camera. It does not reliably tell its left from its right, so the template stops at 180°. Add an angle by adding a line to both panels; use your own pictures with **Add…** on Load Media."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadMedia","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,363],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"files"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[]},{"localized_name":"图片","name":"images","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[42,50]},{"localized_name":"视频","name":"videos","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null},{"localized_name":"音频","name":"audio","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null},{"localized_name":"文件名","name":"names","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null}],"title":"Characters · one group each","properties":{"aux_id":"1Kynx/ComfyUI-Arbor","ver":"c17e607450b1fb2d6376d20911c18857be5d267f","Node name for S&R":"Arbor_LoadMedia"},"widgets_values":["# Mei\narbor:char